  "query_preview": ".. High pressure builds back in across the upper Midwest \nThursday evening, lasting through at least the middle of next week.\nOnly exception will be a 25 to 40% chance for rain on Saturday with \nthe passage of a fast moving short-wave. Otherwise, main forecast \nconcerns for the extended is potential frost/freeze conditions \ntoward the end of the week as high sits overhead and 850 mb \ntemperatures fall to near 0C. There will be a high likelihood of \npatchy frost occurrence several times across the north through \nearly next week, though we could be looking at a more widespread \nfrost/freeze event Sunday into Monday. Will continue to monitor \ntrends for headline potential as we approach the end of the \ngrowing season.",
